   "body": "Fixed on a fork branch: `fix/3785-pool-tooltip` (head `a5f315a3`, on upstream `6eb510f7`) — a pool's account-list tooltip no longer covers its Routing and Stays buttons.\n\n**Root cause.** `internal/gui/assets/plugins/routing/client.js`'s `renderPools` attached the account-list tooltip to the whole row, so anywhere on that row the list covered the Routing and Stays buttons.\n\n**Change.** the tooltip moved to the element that actually lists the accounts behind it (the name element), so the buttons stay reachable; the tip's text is unchanged.\n\n**Verified.** Red: `the new `routing-pool-tooltip.test.cjs` (playwright in a container) against base assets` → `routing-pool-tooltip.test.cjs:54: the row itself carries no tooltip ('acct-a, acct-b' !== null)`\nGreen: `same command → 4/4 (chromium + webkit × en/zh); the neighbours (`stays-strict`, `rate-limited-sink`, `routing-mode-goes`) still pass; `TestCoreScriptBudget` unchanged` → `ℹ pass 4, fail 0`\n\nFull `go test -tags nogui ./...` over round 27's branches: 70 packages ok, 5 red (edit `TestWriteAtomicReadOnlyHardLink`, gateway's five, plugin `TestPluginSOCKSProxy`, provider's synctest fatal in `TestUnreadLoginsWriteErrorsKeepCredentials`, testenv `TestProgram`) — every one of them reproduces identically at base `6eb510f7` in this environment (umask 0027), so none is from this change.\n\nBranch: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/3785-pool-tooltip — no PR opened, this repo takes no external PRs; say the word if you'd rather have the patch inline here.",
